# What Cloud Build does NOT need, and why the upload was 107 MB without it.
#
# The Dockerfile runs `node build.mjs`, which regenerates dist/ from src/ and
# public/. So the two largest directories in this repo are both dead weight in
# the build context:
#
#   raw-assets/  87 MB  the originals that public/assets was optimised FROM.
#                       Nothing in the build reads them.
#   dist/        25 MB  the previous build's output, which the image rebuilds.
#                       Shipping it would also risk baking a stale copy in.
#
# .git is 112 MB and is excluded by gcloud's own defaults, but named here so
# the number is written down next to the others.
#
# Without this the context was 245 MB on disk and 107 MB compressed, which on a
# slow uplink is a build that times out before it starts.

.git/
.gitignore
raw-assets/
dist/
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# Documentation and local tooling: useful to a person, inert to the build.
README.md
LAUNCH.md
CONTENT-REVIEW.md
tools/
deploy/
